# Deborah Milano — Product Naming

When adding or updating Deborah Milano products in catalog scripts, **always set both `nameAr` and `nameEn`**. PATCH with only one field can null the other on the API.

## English (`nameEn`) — global official

Format: `Deborah Milano - [Official Product Name]`

- Match deborahmilano.com / packaging (Title Case, keep `24Ore`, `5-in-1`, `With`, shade at end).
- Examples:
  - `Deborah Milano - Skin Booster Mat Foundation`
  - `Deborah Milano - 24Ore Instant Maxi Volume Mascara With Ceramides Black`
  - `Deborah Milano - Extraordinary 5-in-1 Mascara Blue Navy`

## Arabic (`nameAr`) — Iraqi market

Format: `ديبورا ميلانو - [نوع المنتج بالعربي] [اسم الخط/المنتج بالإنجليزي كما على العبوة]`

- Brand **always** `ديبورا ميلانو` (Arabic letters only — never Latin `a`/`o` in the brand).
- Use Iraqi-familiar product types, then the **official English line name** unchanged:
  - Foundation → `فاونديشن` (not `فونديشن`)
  - Mascara → `ماسكارا`
  - Concealer → `كونسيلر`
  - Lip gloss → `جلوس شفاه`
  - Lip pencil / liner → `قلم شفاه`
  - Brow marker / pencil → `قلم حواجب`
  - Lipstick → `أحمر شفاه` (+ optional Arabic descriptor before line name)
- Shade / variant stays in English at the end (e.g. `Black`, `Chocolate Brown`).
- Examples:
  - `ديبورا ميلانو - فاونديشن Skin Booster Mat`
  - `ديبورا ميلانو - ماسكارا 24Ore Instant Maxi Volume With Ceramides Black`

## Script checklist

```typescript
nameAr: "ديبورا ميلانو - فاونديشن Skin Booster Mat",
nameEn: "Deborah Milano - Skin Booster Mat Foundation",
```

Both fields are required in POST/PATCH payloads for every new Deborah product.
